Appendix J — Cross-Decision Redundancy Estimation Framework

f_redundancy (Section 6.2) is a new metric and needs a worked definition. This appendix provides one.

J.1 Definition

For a sequence of decision cycles  k = 1, \ldots, N :

f_{\text{redundancy}} = \frac{\sum_k \left( C_k - C_k^{\text{essential}} \right)}{\sum_k C_k}

where  C_k  is the total computation performed in cycle  k  and  C_k^{\text{essential}}  is the computation that could not have been avoided given an oracle prior-state cache containing everything from cycle  k-1  that remains valid.

J.2 Why an oracle upper bound is the right first measurement

An oracle cache is unattainable, so f_redundancy as defined is an upper bound on realisable redundancy. That is the correct first measurement because:

· If even the oracle bound is below the 10% threshold, no practical cache can rescue the megakernel case. The investigation terminates with confidence.
· If the oracle bound is high, the next question is how much of it is cheaply realisable—which is a separate experiment.

J.3 Instrumentation for W1

1. Validated prior-state list: camera pose (from odometry), previous obstacle mask, and static terrain features within a defined radius.
2. Essential computation: the minimum work needed to detect new obstacles that were not present or not visible in the previous frame.
3. Measurement method: profile the baseline, classify each operation by whether its inputs are drawn from the prior-state list or from raw stereo data, and sum the time spent on prior-state-derived operations.
4. Cross-check: compare against the fraction of output pixels whose values are unchanged from the previous frame. This provides a sanity bound; f_redundancy should not exceed the unchanged-output fraction by more than a factor to be defined in the protocol.

J.4 Interpretation

f_redundancy (oracle) Interpretation Action
< 10% Little exploitable cross-decision structure Terminate megakernel investigation (Section 6.3)
10–30% Moderate structure Proceed only if f_launch also exceeds 5%, and only with a documented mechanism
30% Substantial structure Proceed to a limited megakernel feasibility study, with the oracle bound stated as an upper limit

The thresholds are provisional [H]. They exist to make the screening decision explicit and reviewable, not to encode a universal truth.

